    feat(distiller): DF-2026-18 nightly session distiller
    
    Adds `duckbrain distill-sessions`: reads the Hermes agent state.db
    (read-only) and, for each session that ended inside the window (default
    24h), extracts bounded, hash-keyed records (decisions, verified findings,
    open items) and writes them under /session/<date>/<session-id>/<hash16>
    in the `sessions` namespace via the repo's own in-process write path
    (rememberTool).
    
    Guarantees:
    - Bounded: <=20 records/session, <=240 chars/statement, <=2000 messages
      scanned/session.
    - Hash-keyed + idempotent: key suffix = sha256(messageHash, recordType,
      statement); skip-if-exists scan makes a rerun over unchanged input
      write zero new records.
    - No transcripts/prompts/secrets: only short extracted statements,
      redacted (key=value secrets, Bearer, sk-*, AKIA*, xox*, JWT, long hex).
    - Cron/system sessions skipped via state.db sessions.source labels
      (cron, kanban, tool).
    - Corrupt transcripts refused loudly (query error / non-text BLOB
      content / non-finite timestamp) with zero partial writes.
    - --dry-run lists what WOULD be written and writes nothing.
    
    Evidence:
    - Fixture suite (new state.db fixture built per test: 2 real sessions +
      1 cron + 1 out-of-window + 1 corrupt): 9/9 green —
      src/cli/session-distiller-df202618.test.ts. RED-proven: with the
      implementation moved aside the suite fails (module not found).
    - Live dry-run against ~/.hermes/state.db (read-only, zero writes;
      verified no `sessions` namespace was created in the production root):
      281 sessions considered, 53 system-skipped, 0 corrupt-refused,
      172 distilled, 802 records would be written — /tmp/df2026-18-dryrun.txt.
    - pnpm tsc --noEmit: clean.
    - prettier --check: new/touched files clean; bin/duckbrain.ts and
      docs/guide/cli-reference.md carry PRE-EXISTING prettier drift at HEAD
      (verified via stash at base 0a415df6), so my edits there were kept
      scoped instead of reformatting unrelated lines.
    - node scripts/docs-check.js: OK (README + 50 docs, fences/links).
    - pnpm test:run: 242/243 files, 2035/2036 tests; the single failure
      (namespace-warmup-aug096 warm-up test, 15s timeout under fleet load)
      is unrelated — isolated rerun passes 16/16 in 9.84s.
    
    Suite totals after this change: 243 suites / 2036 tests (was 242/2027).
    
